    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup optimized to exploit favorable matchups against moderate pitching talent. **Jackson Merrill** stands out as the day\u2019s premier play (75.27) against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez. **Merrill** benefits from a potent combination of a high-ceiling order spot and a slow-working pitcher who provides a significant stolen base opportunity, directly addressing our organizational mandate to maximize speed. Following closely, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) represents a high-leverage start; despite batting lower in the order, his dynamic platoon edge against Michael Lorenzen and the favorable wind conditions in his park environment make him an essential anchor for today's offensive production.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the rotation involved our bench assets, where **Miguel Vargas** (56.16) narrowly missed the final cut. While **Vargas** offers a strong xwOBA profile and high-upside potential against Kumar Rocker, the optimizer prioritized the specific platoon advantages and higher floor projections of **Brayan Rocchio** and **Dominic Smith**. We also held back stalwarts like **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** due to unfavorable matchups against Ranger Suarez, whose profile suppresses their output significantly relative to our starters. While the bench is deep, we are prioritizing high-probability efficiency over name value.\n\nOperational risks for this evening are concentrated on the game featuring **Curtis Mead**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, all of whom face a 33% rain risk. While their matchups against Michael Lorenzen are statistically advantageous\u2014driven by park factors and wind patterns\u2014any potential delay or early rainout poses a cap-preservation threat. Additionally, all lineup assignments remain projected; keep a close eye on the confirmed cards for **Drake Baldwin** and **Jacob Wilson** at the top of the order to ensure they remain in the prime run-producing slots that elevated their scores to the 63 range. **Kyle Tucker** remains a start despite a lower score (57.44) caused by the elite skill of Zack Wheeler, as his raw talent floor remains superior to our bench options.",
